{"authority_basis_atom_keys":["M050-SRC-HUMAN-RULINGS-001::ATOM-HUMAN-RULINGS-DIRECT-0064","M050-SRC-HUMAN-RULINGS-001::ATOM-HUMAN-RULINGS-DIRECT-0065","M050-SRC-PA-001::ATOM-PA-DIRECT-0261","M050-SRC-MSID-GRAMMAR-001::ATOM-MSID-DIRECT-0076"],"canonical_claim":"`Away.Crossing` is both a semantic unit and the parent of Crossing's internal ontology. The dedicated Crossing specification owns its exact phases, execution grammar, adversity, species forks, and tuned procedures. Crossing is uniquely forked among Registers into canonical `Away.Crossing.Mouse`, `Away.Crossing.Rabbit`, and `Away.Crossing.Squirrel` branches because each Core Species has materially different planning, affordance, movement, safety, and failure grammar. These remain branches of one Register, not modifiers to one universal procedure, and must not be flattened into generic `Away.Crossing.Species.*` paths without adjudication.","decision_origin":"provider_reviewed","evidence":{"packet_sha256":"45a5f84becb658d0d77b3588d4bb3c0d76a7b39486a9a063c8530c236ec4fcdc","proposal_response_sha256":"8d7b650f490eee44bb0e8dbec72e26c5d2aebb2806ac63f665208976f6f484d7","review_response_sha256":"6b8f4a644ad5247e7d62b8d29e1f37270572050f5a994f2531bb65da3f7d4f98"},"members":[{"atom_key":"M050-SRC-PA-001::ATOM-PA-DIRECT-0258","disposition":"supporting","effective_claim_sha256":"1b4b4fc9c96fa4249a93f904038d13db957fd821480ce21282b42e85e2ea18cc"},{"atom_key":"M050-SRC-PA-001::ATOM-PA-DIRECT-0259","disposition":"elaboration","effective_claim_sha256":"e28c8c6d920084e6bcf4bb2ef6f3382e705e71adae92e7caa5f3ed5832893e2b"},{"atom_key":"M050-SRC-PA-001::ATOM-PA-DIRECT-0261","disposition":"basis","effective_claim_sha256":"f25090caf6f904830c5ac437e4f23c6fee3b85b704b382022381a129315da68d"},{"atom_key":"M050-SRC-PA-001::ATOM-PA-DIRECT-0283","disposition":"supporting","effective_claim_sha256":"471a991641f1d7c6ec8fd0570668090733aae786d2310a7ba6c27c4bddaf2c41"},{"atom_key":"M050-SRC-PA-001::ATOM-PA-DIRECT-0284","disposition":"supporting","ef